    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d528">

                <pb facs="0590" n="478" sameAs="frus:frus1910/pg478"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Fox to the
                            Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Quito</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1910-06-27"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">June 27, 1910</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 669.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith
                    copies, with translation, of the message<anchor n="1" xml:id="d528-f1"/> of the
                    President of Ecuador submitted to the extraordinary session of Congress, 1910.
                    This document is important, being an analysis of the position of Ecuador in the
                    present conflict with Peru.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Williams C. Fox.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
